What is Multi modal Logistics?
Multi modal logistics is the strategic coordination of freight across multiple modes of transport-rail, road, maritime, and air-within a single contractual framework. Designed to harness the cost efficiency of rail and sea, the speed of air, and the flexibility of road, this model delivers end to end visibility and optimized asset utilisation. The integrated digital platforms that support it enable real time tracking, dynamic rerouting, and integrated customs clearance, allowing shippers to mitigate exceptions and reduce lead times. The approach also substantially lowers carbon emissions, aligning with global sustainability mandates and corporate ESG commitments.
